      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "First, discern that $y$ is the sum of two periodic functions, $\\tan x$ and $\\cot x$. Both $\\tan x$ and $\\cot x$ have a period of $\\pi$, so the domain of $y$ is $\\big({0 \\over \\pi}; \\pi\\big)$. For $x$ in the interval $\\big({0 \\over \\pi}; \\pi\\big)$, it becomes evident that $\\tan x \\neq \\cot x$, and thus they do not overlap. Therefore, the function $\\boxed{\\pi\\text{ units}}$ is the period of $y = \\tan x + \\cot x$.",
