    {
      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To find the period of the function \\( y = \\tan x + \\cot x \\), we need to determine the smallest positive value \\( T \\) such that \\( y( x + T ) = y(x) \\) for all \\( x \\).\n\nFirst, let's recall the periodicity of the tangent and cotangent functions:\n\\[ \\tan(x + \\pi) = \\tan x \\]\n\\[ \\cot(x + \\pi) = \\cot x \\]\n\nNow, we need to add these periodic properties to the function \\( y = \\tan x + \\cot x \\):\n\n\\[ y( x + \\pi ) = \\tan( x + \\pi ) + \\cot( x + \\pi ) \\]\n\\[ y( x + \\pi ) = \\tan x + \\cot x \\]\n\\[ y( x + \\pi ) = y( x ) \\]\n\nThus, \\( y = \\tan x + \\cot x \\) has a period of \\( \\pi \\).\n\nConclusion: The period of \\( y = \\tan x + \\cot x \\) is \\( \\boxed{\\pi} \\).",
